<title>SWEDEN: Skandia sells British properties.</title>
<headline>Skandia sells British properties.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish insurance company Skandia said on Monday it will sell an office building in London's Trafalgar Square for 450 million crowns to an Asian buyer.  </p>
<p>The building was part of a real estate portfolio acquired from Reinhold International in 1989.</p>
<p>Skandia said the sale will not affect the Skandia group's results or net asset value.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
</text>
